\title{Locally Compact Space}
\taxon{Definition}
\p{
    A topological space #{X} is \strong{locally compact at #{x\in X}} if
    there exists a [compact](def-005R) subspace #{K\subseteq X} that is a
    [neighborhood](def-005L) of #{x}. The space is \strong{locally compact} if
    it is locally compact at every point.
}
\p{
    This definition does not include the [Hausdorff](def-005S) condition. In a
    different convention, some texts use \em{locally compact} to mean locally
    compact and Hausdorff. Outside the Hausdorff setting, several common
    formulations of local compactness need not be equivalent.
}
